; TONE/PLAYSOUND/STOPSOUND: fire-and-forget sound effects, like
; MOUSEPOS/JOYSTICK? never pausing the script. Only audible in the
; real app (SDL2's audio device) -- no sound hardware in the headless
; test driver, so these are silent no-ops there.

TONE 440 0.3      ; play a 440Hz (concert A) tone for 0.3 seconds
WAIT 0.5
TONE 880 0.3      ; an octave up
WAIT 0.5

; A little ascending scale, one note per iteration, each note
; replacing whatever's still playing from the note before it (TONE
; always clears the queue first -- only one sound plays at a time).
TO scale
  FOR [step 0 7] [
    TONE 220 * POWER 1.06 :step 0.15
    WAIT 0.2
  ]
END

; PLAYSOUND "path plays a WAV file the same fire-and-forget way,
; converting its sample rate/format to match the device if needed.
; STOPSOUND cuts off whatever TONE/PLAYSOUND is still playing.
; sample.wav/sample2.wav (free-use) are alongside this file to try it
; with -- run these two lines from the same directory as sound.logo:
;
; PLAYSOUND "sample.wav
; WAIT 2
; STOPSOUND
